    "title": "CVS Pharmacy Holiday Hours and Schedule",
    "text": "January 2, 2026 3 min Read jetcityimage / Getty Images Commitment to Our Readers GOBankingRates' editorial team is committed to bringing you unbiased reviews and information. We use data-driven methodologies to evaluate financial products and services - our reviews and ratings are not influenced by advertisers. You can read more about our editorial guidelines and our products and services review methodology. 20 YearsHelping You Live Richer Reviewed by Experts Trusted by Millions of Readers If you’re planning a quick trip to CVS around a holiday — whether to grab prescriptions, pick up household essentials or snag last-minute gifts — it’s smart to check store hours ahead of time. While most CVS stores remain open on major holidays, hours can vary by location, especially for pharmacy services. CVS Regular Store Hours Most CVS stores are open daily from 8:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m., and some 24-hour locations remain open around the clock. Pharmacy counters typically operate from 9:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. but often close early or remain closed on major holidays. What About MinuteClinic Hours? MinuteClinic locations inside CVS stores may also adjust hours on holidays or close entirely. To confirm: Use the MinuteClinic locator Call your local CVS to ask about nurse practitioner availability CVS Major Holiday Schedule for 2026 CVS caters to its customers even during holidays, with most stores staying open to meet your emergency and last-minute needs. Here’s a look at CVS holiday hours for 2026: Holiday Date Hours New Year’s Day Thursday, Jan. 1 Typically open, may have reduced hours Martin Luther King, Jr. Day Monday, Jan. 19 Open Presidents Day Monday, Feb. 16 Open Easter Sunday Sunday, April 5 Typically open, may have reduced hours Memorial Day Monday, May 25 Open Juneteenth National Independence Day Friday, June 19 Open Independence Day Saturday, July 4 Open Labor Day Monday, Sept. 7 Open Columbus Day/Indigenous Peoples Day Monday, Oct. 12 Open Veterans Day Wednesday, Nov. 11 Open Thanksgiving Day Thursday, Nov. 26 Typically open, may have reduced hours Christmas Day Friday, Dec. 25 Typically open, may have reduced hours Tips for Shopping at CVS During the Holidays Check pharmacy hours early: Some locations operate with reduced staff or limited pickup windows. Shop early in the day: Lines are typically shorter in the morning. Stock up on essentials: Items like sunscreen, allergy meds and beverages often sell out fast. Use ExtraCare deals: Promotions and digital coupons may still apply even on holidays. Use self-checkout: To save you time when lines are long. More Holiday Hours Apple Costco Dollar General Kohl’s Lowe’s Macy’s Safeway Starbucks Target Trader Joe’s Walgreens Walmart CVS Holiday Hours: FAQ Here are answers to some frequently asked questions about CVS Pharmacy holiday hours. Is CVS open on all holidays? Yes, most CVS locations are open every day of the year, including holidays. However, pharmacy and clinic hours may vary significantly. Are CVS pharmacies open on Christmas or Thanksgiving? Some pharmacies close on major holidays like Christmas Day or Thanksgiving, while retail stores may remain open. Check local listings for details. Can I refill or pick up prescriptions on a holiday? In many cases, yes — but not all pharmacies are open on holidays. Use the CVS app or website to confirm before heading out. Are 24-hour CVS locations open during holidays? Yes. 24-hour CVS stores typically stay open year-round, but pharmacy counters inside may have different hours. Is the MinuteClinic open on holidays? Some MinuteClinic locations may close or operate on limited hours during holidays. Always check the MinuteClinic locator for up-to-date availability. Do CVS ExtraCare coupons still work on holidays? Yes. CVS ExtraCare and digital coupons usually remain valid during holidays, both in-store and through the app. Cynthia Measom and Elizabeth Constantineau contributed to the reporting for this article. All holiday hours were confirmed as of Dec. 26, 2025. Check with your local retailer to confirm specific hours. Hours and policies are subject to change. Editorial Note: This content is not provided by any entity covered in this article. Any opinions, analyses, reviews, ratings or recommendations expressed in this article are those of the author alone.",
